(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "ADR-2608197200")
  (:adr/title "closing: nine landings on one defect class — a check that could not measure, reporting what a clean measurement reports")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-19")
  (:adr/tags "closing handoff detectors evidence-floor co-scientist")
  (:adr/body
  "## What this session was

A `/loop` at 30-minute cadence, asked to raise maturity and performance by the
Google Co-Scientist method. Iterations 25–33 ran at workspace scope. Every one of
them found the same defect, in a different place:

**something that could not measure produced the output of something that measured
and found nothing.**

## Landed on origin/main

| ADR | What |
|---|---|
| 2608196300 | `verify-kip-quorum` exited 0 on an empty subject. Now exit 3 + a `VERIFIED` line; registered |
| 2608196400 | `verify-app-content-address` told a human about 80 violations and a machine about 0; its refusal exited 1, not 2. Registered |
| 2608196500 | The 6300 fix broke its dependent — `verify-kip-coverage` refused on exit 3. Exit 3 now proceeds |
| 2608196600 | `verify-shadow-source-paths`: **73 fail -> 24 fail + 49 warn.** Two thirds were conditional on taking the fix it suggested |
| 2608196700 | `verify-vendored-copies`: `app.cljc` parsed as a namespace. **30 of 76** re-diagnosed |
| 2608196800 | The tick recorded a refusal as `ok` and marked **337 findings RESOLVED**. Exit >=2 is now `:inconclusive` |
| 2608196900 | That refusal was a floor whose premise was falsified in 3 days: 16 appviews migrated off Svelte. Floor 150 -> 50 |
| 2608197000 | `gen-appview-page-summary --names <repo>` matched nothing and printed `0 differ`. A fix that could not fix |
| 2608197100 | Five appview pages now report the routes they are served at |

Also landed: `etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-app-explorer` `e899b55c` (a `:source-path`
resolving to `orgs/orgs/...`, five files requiring `kotoba.datom` in a build that
could not compile), and five `cloud-itonami` page repairs. All six child landings
are `identical` to their default branch; all six west pins verified present in
`origin/main:manifest/west.yml`.

**Detector precision, measured:** shadow-source-paths 73 -> 24 real,
vendored-copies 76 -> 46 real. Roughly **80 of 149** findings across those two were
noise a human would have triaged by hand.

## Resume point — start here

1. **91 appview repositories still lie about their routes** (287 standing findings;
   15 of them belong to the five repaired and resolve on the next sync). The
   per-repo procedure is in ADR-2608197100, including both traps: west remotes are
   named after the org, and **zsh does not word-split**.
2. **The shared checkout is ~30 commits behind `origin/main`** and cannot
   fast-forward: a neighbouring session has `90-docs/kaizen/kaiyu-kaizen.ledger.edn`
   modified in the working tree, and one stash (`kaiyu-kaizen woke-tick lines
   preserved…`) is theirs. **Both were left untouched.** The pins landed regardless;
   `west update` picks them up when that tree syncs.
   ⚠ A consequence worth knowing: while that tree is stale, the PreToolUse guard
   `west-pin-verify-guard.cljs` **blocks every `git push` issued from it**, because
   it evaluates the checkout's own `west.yml` (7 entries regress against main) and
   not what the push actually carries. This ADR was pushed from a worktree cut at
   the current `origin/main` instead. The guard is right to be fail-closed; the
   message just describes a candidate nobody proposed.
3. **Three `orgs/`-reading verifiers remain unregistered**:
   `d1-kotobase-migration` (17s, real output, no SCANNED protocol),
   `duplicate-registrations` (55s, 10 `gh` calls, exit 0 — needs its own reading
   before it is trusted), `kotoba-pages` (blocked: Playwright's browser is not
   installed). Registry is at 17 entries, 15 with live state, 2,293 standing findings.
4. **`verify-artifact-path-policy` skips 26 of its 27 subjects** and needs an
   evidence floor before it is worth gating.
5. **Three verifiers have a twin** under `scripts/fleet-ci/gates/` (`capital-pools`,
   `kotobase-persistence-policy`, `source-nul-bytes`); one copy of each has to win.
6. **Upstream, unanswered:** `kotoba-lang/amu#625` (missing
   `kernel-compare-exchange-u32`, 5 of 11 aiueos value-runtime failures) and
   `#626` (export symbol rule, 3 more). Both open, one comment each, both mine.
7. **Owner decisions still open:** make `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-tcp` public (would
   restore aiueos fleet assertion coverage 20% -> 100%), install-to-internal-disk,
   real SPKI pins for kotobase.net / api.murakumo.cloud, physical-hardware boot.

## What I would tell the next agent about method

- **Measure before fixing.** Two hypotheses about the vendored-copy burst were
  wrong; each cost one command and would have cost a wrong fix.
- **Verify against `origin/main`, not your worktree.** Several times the shared
  checkout was behind and a run silently used the old script.
- **`cmd | head` returns head's exit code.** It reported `exit=0` for a script that
  exits 2, twice today.
- **Remove exactly what you created, never its parent.** `rm -rf <worktree>/orgs`
  deleted 229,346 tracked files; `git status` caught it.
- **An index.lock that comes straight back is not stale.** Three were; the fourth
  was a neighbouring session committing continuously. Retry, do not clear.
- **A floor is a claim about the world.** Size it against the threat it names, not
  against the population that existed the afternoon it was written.")))
